reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/combat/notes.md:53:## Disagreements with the old Journal Club record
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/combat/notes.md:62:- EAU 2026 (section 5.2.7.a) attributes "relative risk of AUR reduced by 68%, BPH-related surgery by 71% and symptom deterioration by 41% versus tamsulosin" and "13 patients treated for 4 years" to its reference 297 in the extracted text, but that number points to an Athanasopoulos 2003 alpha-blocker plus anticholinergic trial. The CombAT percentages could not be confirmed from CombAT sources I read and are not used on the page; the registry's yearly counts imply an absolute risk reduction of 7.7% (NNT about 13), which matches the EAU text.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/combat/notes.md:63:- The AUA 2026 guideline text says CombAT "did not show clinically important differences in symptoms or quality of life between combination therapy and dutasteride alone"; the page attributes this to the AUA review.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/combat/notes.md:64:- The FDA approval date (June 14, 2010) comes from the openFDA Drugs@FDA record; confirm on the accessdata page if the claim gate requires fda.gov HTML.
