reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:15:Guideline texts read for this trial: ASCRS 2023 fecal incontinence guideline (`reports/audit-v2/sources-local/pdfs-2026-10-10/ASCRS-Fecal-Incontinence-2023.pdf`) and ACOG Practice Bulletin 210 (`/Users/joyboy/Downloads/acog-practice-bulletin-no-210-fecal-incontinence.pdf`). Neither cites CAPABLe (ASCRS cites only Markland 2015 on biofeedback protocol; ACOG 210 predates the paper), so the page has no "Guidelines and approvals" section. One web search for a guideline citing CAPABLe found none. No FDA action rests on the trial.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:24:## Disagreements and cautions
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:26:### Other WARWIKI pages
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:31:- Line 154: the page says only that clinicians should counsel about constipation risk. The source gives constipation in 33/88 (38%) and 44/86 (51%) of the two loperamide groups versus 5/42 (12%) and 19/84 (23%) of the placebo groups, P < 0.001 (Results text). The loperamide row at line 146 cites only FIRM (29% versus 10%).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:33:- Line 154 "the combined intervention versus either component alone" matches the intention-to-treat result (P = 0.09 and 0.33). The per-protocol analyses (P = 0.017 and 0.018) are smaller than the minimally important difference and are not mentioned; this is not an error.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:37:No number disagrees: n = 300, 24-week St Mark's (Vaizey) change, DOI, journal and year match. Differences of wording only:
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:39:- `name`: "Controlling Anal incontinence by Performing Anal exercises with Biofeedback or Loperamide" is the acronym expansion in the PMC manuscript; the published Lancet title and PubMed use "Controlling faecal incontinence in women by performing anal exercises with biofeedback or loperamide: a randomised clinical trial". The page H1 uses the manuscript's expansion and the reference line uses the published title.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:43:### Internal inconsistencies in the source (worth knowing before the claim gate)
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/capable/notes.md:54:- The Lancet publisher page was not opened; page numbers and Table numbers refer to the PMC manuscript.
