reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/cheetah/notes.md:30:## Disagreements and discrepancies
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/cheetah/notes.md:35:- Registry number: the primary report prints NCT03700749, which is FALCON's record. ChEETAh is NCT03980652 (clinicaltrials.gov title "Cheetah - Sterile Glove and Clean Instrument Change at the Time of Wound Closure to Reduce Surgical Site Infection"; the cost-effectiveness paper and the protocol give NCT03980652). The file uses NCT03980652.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/cheetah/notes.md:42:- Group author name: the Lancet article says "NIHR Global Research Health Unit on Global Surgery"; the 2024 paper says "NIHR Global Health Research Unit on Global Surgery". Each citation uses the form printed on its own article (PubMed's CollectiveName matches).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/cheetah/notes.md:43:- The Results state recruitment ended 8 months ahead of the projected completion date (clusters) and 3 months before the projected date (participants); the page uses only the first.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/cheetah/notes.md:44:- Enz et al. print the intervention rate as 931 (16.0%) of 5,789 and name Ademuyiwa as first author of the trial; the Lancet article is under the group name.
