reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/lift/notes.md:35:## Disagreements with WARWIKI pages
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/lift/notes.md:41:3. "40/140 treated men received a catheter by site protocol; 68/100 of the others avoided catheterization after a voiding trial." Neither the 3-year nor the 5-year report contains these counts. Both state that 32% required catheterization for a failed voiding trial (mean catheter duration 0.9 days over the whole cohort; 5-year PDF p4), which fits 32/100 but not 40/140. Unverified without the 2013 full text.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/lift/notes.md:42:4. Table row "3 mo ... Qmax +4.4 mL/s" is the lift-arm figure from the abstract; the randomized comparison reports 4.28 (lift) versus 1.98 mL/s (sham). Not an error, but the sham comparison is absent.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/lift/notes.md:58:- The old bottom line ("at the cost of more modest flow gains") is a comparison with resection that this trial did not test; the page leaves it to the BPH6 and EAU paragraph.
