reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:33:- Eligibility and washout details on the page come from the registry record text.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:39:- The label prints different "any adverse reaction" figures in two places (92% versus 61% for at least one reaction in the text; 84.2% versus 36.3% for reactions in at least 1% and above placebo in Table 5). Neither is used in the file or page.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:40:- The AUA guideline's ecchymosis figures (80.0% versus 26.0%) equal the label's hematoma plus ecchymosis rows (65.5 + 14.5; 19.2 + 6.8), so the report appears to have combined them. The page uses the label's separate rows.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:45:- EAU PDF page numbers (81, 82, 84) are also the printed page numbers. AUA page numbers are the printed numbers on the guideline document.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:46:- The EAU guideline states that CCH was withdrawn from the European market by its manufacturer; the page reports that as the guideline's statement.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:55:- The Cochrane review cited on WARWIKI pages: not opened.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:57:## Disagreements with WARWIKI pages (`grep -rln IMPRESS docs`)
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/impress/notes.md:80:- Sites and countries beyond the registry listing (29 US, 5 Australian sites per record).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:5:- Primary report: Peters KM et al., J Urol 2009;182(3):1055-1061, doi 10.1016/j.juro.2009.05.045, PMID 19616802. **Abstract only** (PubMed efetch). Full text is paywalled (jurology.com returned 403; Europe PMC and Unpaywall list no open copy; no local copy under `reports/audit-v2/sources-local`, `/Users/joyboy/Documents/Medicine` or `/Users/joyboy/Downloads`). Citation checked against Crossref (authors, volume, issue, pages) and PubMed (electronic date 2009-07-18).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:10:- FDA 510(k) database page for K052025 (Urgent PC Neuromodulation System, Uroplasty, decision date October 17, 2005). The summary PDF itself returned HTML, so indications were not read; only the date and applicant are used.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:12:- Secondary: PubMed search snippet and Urology Times news article (not used for any number on the page or file).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:18:- Urology Times news article: reports 35/43 (80%) versus 23/42 (55%) and a physician-assessed cure of 75% versus 56%; secondary source, so excluded. Note the abstract's 79.5% implies 35/44, not 35/43, so that article's denominator is suspect.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:22:- Primary report read at abstract level only: `met: null` on the two primary or key-secondary results; the noninferiority margin and the exact prespecified primary endpoint could not be confirmed from the paper. `design.type: noninferiority` and the voids/day primary come from the registry text. The page states the registry's primary outcome as "registered", not as the paper's.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:24:- Harm counts (6/50 versus 4/50; serious 0/50) are registry values; the abstract only says no serious adverse events or device malfunctions. The news article's claim that constipation and dry mouth were less frequent with PTNS (P values not given) could not be checked.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:25:- Discrepancy between sources on responders continuing PTNS: 33 (J Urol 2010 abstract) versus 35 (registry and ICS abstracts). The page uses 33; the file notes the registry's 35. The 2010 abstract has 32 and 25 completing 6 and 12 months; registry lists 25 completing 12 months.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:31:## Disagreements with WARWIKI pages
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/orbit/notes.md:33:- No page under `docs/` mentions OrBIT, its DOI or the Peters 2009 report (grep for OrBIT, "Overactive Bladder Innovative", both DOIs). Nothing to correct.
