reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pae-vs-turp/notes.md:36:Pages citing it: `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04m-bph-male-luts/prostate-artery-embolization.mdx` (Abt 2018 as ref 31, Abt 2021 as ref 17, post hoc as ref 21, 5-year as ref 25), `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04m-bph-male-luts/index.mdx` (5-year as ref 17), and `docs/01-foundations/anatomy-physiology/genitalia/prostate-seminal-vesicle.mdx` (5-year as ref 33). `bladder-outlet-obstruction.mdx` and `turp.mdx` do not cite it.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pae-vs-turp/notes.md:38:Disagreements and items to recheck (no other file was edited):
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pae-vs-turp/notes.md:40:1. `prostate-artery-embolization.mdx`, table "Comparison with TURP", row "Retreatment at 2 yr": TURP column says "Not reported". The 2021 report (Results, "Dropouts and re-treatments") gives other surgical procedures in 5 of 51 TURP patients (10%) versus 1 PAE patient (2%) in addition to the 10 PAE-to-TURP conversions, and 2 TURP patients (4.3%) on antimuscarinics at 24 months. (The Discussion states 7.8% for TURP; the source disagrees with itself.)
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pae-vs-turp/notes.md:42:3. Same page, text after the table: "TURP was superior for IPSS (difference 2.88, p = 0.047)" matches the 2021 abstract, but the page does not say that this was a protocol-defined secondary comparison without correction for multiple testing and that the primary endpoint (12 weeks) did not establish noninferiority. This is an omission, not a numeric conflict.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pae-vs-turp/notes.md:54:4 reports, 25 results, 14 harms, 13 delivery facts (file); 6 references (page).
