reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/merit/notes.md:28:Pages citing MERIT: `docs/05-special-populations/05e-womens-health/recurrent-uti.mdx`, `docs/01-foundations/pharmacology/infection-prophylaxis/non-antibiotic-uti-prevention.mdx`, `docs/01-foundations/pharmacology/infection-prophylaxis/uti-suppressive-prophylactic.mdx`. No old Journal Club record exists. Numbers on `recurrent-uti.mdx` line 148 (598 women, 150/294 [51.0%] versus 161/289 [55.7%], risk difference −5 points, 95% CI −13 to 3) agree with the source (PDF p1, p7 Table 2).
