reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:13:Every DOI above resolved on Crossref with matching authors, journal, volume, issue and pages; PMIDs came from Europe PMC. No source could not be opened. The Springer page for the IUJ report redirected to a cookie handshake, so the PMC full text was used instead. Page locators for the Lancet report are the printed page numbers of the online-first PDF (1 to 12), not the journal pages 381 to 392. Registry: ISRCTN60695184 (no NCT number, so `nct` is null and `registry` carries the ISRCTN).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:29:## Disagreements with WARWIKI pages
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:31:- `docs/01-foundations/tools/biomaterials/biological-grafts/porcine-sis.mdx` line 87: "PROSPECT randomized program (1,348 women followed to 6 years)". The 6-year report retained 65% of the 1,348 randomized women (IUJ 2023, Results, Participants and treatment); the next sentence of that page already says "about 65% response", so only the parenthetical is loose.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:33:- `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04g-prolapse-repair/mesh-graft-augmented-repairs.mdx` line 53: "prolapse symptom scores ... were similar across randomized comparisons" at six years. True at 6 years (mesh trial mean difference 0.85, 95% CI -0.05 to 1.75; Table 1), but the 4-year mesh-trial POP-SS was higher after mesh (mean difference 1.01, 95% CI 0.20 to 1.83; P=0.015; below the 2-point threshold). The page does not mention 4 years, so no conflict unless the 4-year result is added.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:36:## Disagreements with the old Journal Club record
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:50:- `status.claimsChecked` and `clinicalReview` are null as instructed. `npm run lint:trials` logic was run against this file and page in a scratch copy and passed.
