reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pinnacle/notes.md:40:- `/Users/joyboy/Documents/WARWIKI/warwiki/docs/04-surgical-techniques/04m-bph-male-luts/aquablation.mdx` (comparison sentence citing the Akgul review): "2.5% for Optilume BPH at 2 years". The 2-year PINNACLE report gives surgical reintervention 3/100 (3%) (Discussion). The same page's table gives 3/100. `greenlight-pvp.mdx` line 184 also says "2.5% at 2 yr". Akgul was not opened; the 2.5% does not appear in the PINNACLE papers.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/pinnacle/notes.md:42:- `optilume-bph.mdx` sentence on crossover: "Twenty sham participants crossed over to active treatment before 12 months" is correct (SSED p 16 of 46). The page's Efficacy table lists "Sexual function ... preserved" for the sham column as "-"; the paper does report sham sexual scores (Table 3). Not an error.
