reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/tomus/notes.md:24:## Reconciliation with existing WARWIKI pages
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/tomus/notes.md:26:The TOMUS passages in `docs/03-clinical-conditions/03a-storage-incontinence/sui-female.mdx`, `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04f-incontinence-procedures/procedures/female-slings-suspensions.mdx`, `retropubic-midurethral-sling.mdx`, `transobturator-midurethral-sling.mdx`, and `docs/01-foundations/tools/instruments/urethral-specialty/midurethral-sling-trocars.mdx` give the source's 12-month composites (80.8% versus 77.7%; 62.2% versus 55.8%) and distinguish the 12-month objective equivalence finding. The stated 5-year cohort figures (404/597; 51.3% versus 43.4%) also match. No numerical contradiction was found in those passages.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/tomus/notes.md:36:- “Route is chosen by patient anatomy and risk tolerance rather than efficacy” overstates the evidence. Objective equivalence was demonstrated only at 12 months; subjective equivalence was not, and neither composite met equivalence at 24 months (Albo 2012, Figure 2).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/tomus/notes.md:41:- The schema has no `equivalence` design type; `noninferiority` is used as the nearest allowed type, while `design.description`, the result notes, and the page state that this was a **two-sided equivalence** trial with a ±12-point margin.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/tomus/notes.md:44:- No FDA approval or clearance claim was included; none was checked against FDA records for this page.
