reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rezum/notes.md:47:## Disagreements and checks on other WARWIKI pages
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rezum/notes.md:49:Pages searched: `grep -rln "Rezūm\|Rezum" docs`. Statements checked against the sources read; most agree. Differences:
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rezum/notes.md:51:1. `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04m-bph-male-luts/aquablation.mdx`, line 172: "the Akgul review reported surgical reintervention of 13.6% for UroLift and 11.1% for Rezūm at 5 years". In the Rezūm II 5-year report, surgical retreatment was 4.4% (journal p720, Figure 3) and 11.1% was the share who started BPH medication (p721, Figure 3). The 11.1% is a medication-initiation figure, so labelling it surgical reintervention misstates the pivotal trial (the Akgul review itself was not opened). The same page's table (line 204, "11.1% at 5 yr (Akgul review); 4.4% at 5 yr (pivotal trial, EAU 2026)") sets the two side by side without saying the 11.1% is medication.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rezum/notes.md:53:   - Efficacy table: Qmax "44% improvement" and BPH Impact Index "48%" at 5 years are the abstract's figures; the 5-year paper's Results text gives 49% (14.0 ± 5.4 mL/s from 9.9 ± 2.2) and 45% (2.2 ± 1.4). The paper disagrees with itself (journal p715 versus p720).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rezum/notes.md:70:- FDA clearance dates for K160417 (2016-03-17), K180237 (2018-02-27), K191505 (2019-08-02), K190093 (2019-03-25) and K262460 (2026-09-03) come from the openFDA 510(k) API only; they are not on the page. The page cites K150786 and K250584, each read as a PDF on accessdata.fda.gov.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rezum/notes.md:71:- The page's EAU bullet does not use a `<Rec>` badge because the EAU text gives no graded recommendation for WVTT.
