reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:18:Every DOI resolved on Crossref with matching authors, year, journal, volume and pages (the AUA DOI after a retry). No Rec badge or numbers were taken from an AI summary; the WebFetch/WebSearch summaries were used only to find the PMID and were not used for any value.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:22:- The primary paper's full text could not be opened (paywalled; publisher page blocked). `status.sourceRead` and the primary `source.level` are therefore `abstract`. Primary-report numbers beyond the abstract (denominators, month-9 and month-13.5 proportions, IIEF-EF change, all harms, completion) come from the ClinicalTrials.gov results record and are labeled so in each locator. The registry record has not been confirmed against the paper's tables. Please compare the harms with the paper's adverse-event table if a copy arrives (registry combines double-blind treatment and washout, and lists non-serious events at a zero threshold).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:23:- The primary paper's own adverse-event wording (for example "no new safety signals", quoted by Patel 2015) was not read in the primary text, so the page does not use it.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:25:- Penile length: abstract (Brock 2015 and the primary abstract) gives 4.1 mm (95% CI 0.4-7.8, P = 0.032); the registry's posted analysis gives 4.20 (0.47-7.93; P = 0.028). The file and page use the paper's figure.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:26:- Age limit: the primary abstract says "≤ 68 yr"; Moncada, Patel and Montorsi 2016 say "<68". The page says "68 or younger" (primary abstract). Brock's abstract also says "≤68".
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:29:- Relation to `sildenafil-pivotal` (type `extends`) is a judgment: the site's pivotal sildenafil file is on-demand treatment of established ED, REACTT is the post-prostatectomy rehabilitation question. Drop it if the editor wants only direct lineage.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:30:- FDA: no approval statement included; REACTT did not lead to a labeled rehabilitation indication that I could verify at fda.gov, and I did not check, so the page omits any FDA claim.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:31:- Guidelines: the EAU Sexual and Reproductive Health guideline (which the WARWIKI ED page cites as EAU 2026) is not among the local copies, so its statements are not on the page. The EAU Prostate Cancer text is discussion without a strength rating, so no Rec badge. Other guidelines (NCCN survivorship, SMSNA, ASCO) were not available locally.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/reactt/notes.md:36:- Cochrane review of penile rehabilitation (Philippou 2018, CD012414) and the AUA meta-analysis: pooled analyses, not REACTT reports (AUA pooled RR is quoted on the page from the local guideline).
