reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:46:## Internal inconsistencies in the sources (how I handled them)
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:65:Sources read in full (folder `reports/audit-v2/sources-local/pdfs-2026-10-19/`): `UPSTREAM-Drake-2020-Accepted-Manuscript.pdf` (author accepted manuscript of the Eur Urol 2020 primary report; locators are PDF pages, which are manuscript pages plus one), `UPSTREAM-Drake-2020-Tables.pdf` (Tables 1 to 4) and `UPSTREAM-Drake-2020-Figure-1-CONSORT.pdf`; `UPSTREAM-Clout-5-Year-2025-EUF.pdf` (Eur Urol Focus 2025, version of record; locators are PDF pages) and `UPSTREAM-5-Year-HTA-2025.pdf` (HTA 2025;29(26); locators are printed page and table numbers). Figure 2 of the primary report (`.tif`) could not be decoded here, so its values are not used. The supplements (Supplementary Tables 1 to 6) were not supplied. `source.level` is now `full-text` and `source.checked` is 2026-10-19 for `upstream-2020`, `upstream-2025` and `upstream-2025-hta`; `status.sourceRead` is `full-text`. The statements above in this file that the primary and 5-year reports were read at abstract level are superseded.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:75:7. Page, Design: the "8,671 screened, 1,482 eligible, 55% of those eligible" sentence is replaced by the CONSORT breakdown (5,910 not eligible, 662 declined, 1,279 not included for an unidentified reason; 820 randomized). The 1,482 comes from the HTA 2020 text and equals 820 + 662, ignoring the 1,279; it is no longer printed.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:76:8. Page, Design: added unfitness for surgery and unwillingness to comply to the exclusions, prior conservative or medical therapy to eligibility, and noninferiority declared when the upper limit was below 1 point.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:78:10. HTA 2025 citation now carries volume and issue (2025;29(26)); date locator updated to the title page ("published July 2025"; no day given).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:79:11. Locators: the abstract locators on the three updated reports were replaced by page, table or section locators.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:86:- Page: new 5-year paragraphs (surgery, secondary outcomes, interactions, costs), the journal report's interaction p value, the quality-control finding, the adverse-event attribution, 5-year deaths and the expanded limitations.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:88:### Disagreements and anomalies found in the full texts
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:90:1. **Post hoc surgery-by-arm interaction, p value.** The Eur Urol manuscript gives p < 0.001 ("surgery being potentially more beneficial in the Routine Care arm", Figure 2, Supplementary Table 4). The HTA 2020 report (already in the file) gives an interaction difference of 2.93 (95% CI 0.86 to 5.01), p = 0.006, falling to p = 0.283 as treated. Both are shown on the page. The 5-year HTA found the same direction but not significant (2.26, p = 0.118).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:91:2. **Sample size.** The manuscript states 800 men (margin 1, SD 5, 20% attrition, 80% power); the HTA 2020 file states 310 per arm inflated to 388 per arm (776). The page keeps the HTA figures.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:92:3. **Received urodynamics.** Manuscript: 353 (83%) of 427 and 28 (7%) of 393; HTA 2020 Table 6 (in the file): 353/421 (84%) and 360/388 (93%) received the allocated pathway. Different denominators, not a conflict; both are on the page.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:93:4. **Adjusted analysis sample.** The manuscript gives 641 (78%) analysable after baseline adjustment (328 versus 313). The page's earlier 340/329 are the 18-month IPSS counts (Table 2); both are now stated.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:96:7. **Surgery since 18 months.** The Eur Urol Focus paper says an additional "~56" procedures (the symbol is garbled in the extraction) came between 18 months and 5 years (347 minus 291). The HTA gives 66 additional cases in Table 8 and the text, 65 in the scientific summary (454 non-surgical + 281 + 66 = 801). Not used on the page.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/upstream/notes.md:98:9. **HTA 2025 table labels.** Tables 21 and 22 label the urodynamics group n = 393 and routine care n = 427, which appear swapped relative to randomization (427 and 393); group n values from those tables are not used. The M653/M662/M672 code names are printed with "necrotising enterocolitis" for NEC; the page says "not elsewhere classified" (the printed text of section 3.5.1 reads "NEC").
