reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/stitch/notes.md:37:- `docs/01-foundations/surgical-principles/incisions-closure.mdx` line 76: "the large-bite arm used 10-mm bites/spacing"; source: bites "of at least 1 cm" and spacing of 1 cm (Lancet PDF p2, Procedures). Same page, same paragraph: "Emergency laparotomy was excluded" is correct only in the sense that only elective surgery was included (PDF p6, Discussion). Line 74: "Other complication rates did not differ significantly" matches Table 3 (PDF p5).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/stitch/notes.md:38:- `docs/01-foundations/tools/instruments/forceps/bonney.mdx` line 55 and `docs/01-foundations/anatomy-physiology/donor-sites/abdominal-wall.mdx` line 272: 13-year figures (34% versus 49%, HR 0.61, 0.43–0.86, median censoring 8 years, mean hernia 25 versus 43 mm, repair similar) match the JAMA Surg abstract; "randomized 559 patients" matches the abstract but not the original 560 (see above). Bonney line 55 states the control suture as "looped polydioxanone on a 48-mm needle" (abstract) without the size 1 gauge, which is fine.
