reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/vue/notes.md:28:## Inconsistencies inside the source (how I handled them)
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/vue/notes.md:31:2. Table 16 percentages do not follow the printed N: 14/262 = 5.3% (printed 5.4%), 5/262 = 1.9% (printed 2.0%). The file and page quote the printed n (%) without a numerator/denominator pair. 16/269 = 5.9% is correct.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/vue/notes.md:34:5. Vault urinary incontinence: the text gives any incontinence as 30.8% (abdominal) versus 24.0% (vaginal); Table 30 gives 32/85 (37.6%) versus 25/86 (29.1%). Not used on the page.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/vue/notes.md:36:7. Recruitment start is March 2013 (scientific summary) or January 2013 (Chapter 3 text); 45 centers (Chapters 4, 7) versus 36 vault-recruiting centers (Chapter 6). The page gives March 2013 and omits the center count.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/vue/notes.md:47:- Not verified: the arithmetic of every percentage in the source tables (I recounted those in the file against their numerators and denominators; only the Table 16 items above disagree); the HTA's lifetime Markov model (Chapter 9) was read in summary only and is not on the page.
