reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/scandinavian-urethroplasty/notes.md:33:## Disagreements between the two reports
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/scandinavian-urethroplasty/notes.md:35:1. Wound infection: primary Table 7 and text report 3/75 (4.0%) wound infections in the tEPA arm at catheter removal (grade II in two, IIIa in one). Holm 2026 section 3.2 says "None of the patients developed a wound infection." The page and file follow the primary report.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/scandinavian-urethroplasty/notes.md:40:## Disagreements and checks on other WARWIKI pages (no pages edited)
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/scandinavian-urethroplasty/notes.md:43:- Same page: "reduced glans stiffness ... 13/70 (19%) after transecting EPA versus 5/74 (6.8%) after BMG, and perceived erect penile shortening by 18/70 (26%) versus 4/74 (5.4%)". The percentages match primary Table 4 (PDF p4), but the 70 and 74 denominators are not printed in either report (inferred from the 144 completers and the percentages).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/scandinavian-urethroplasty/notes.md:44:- Same page: "Postoperative scrotal/perineal hematoma ... 18/75 (24%) ... 3/76 (3.9%)": matches primary Table 7 (PDF p5). "median stricture length was 1 cm in each arm": matches Table 3 (10 mm in each arm).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/scandinavian-urethroplasty/notes.md:48:- No page states the trial's co-primary endpoints, the planned sample of 300 or the early stop; `urethral-reconstruction-principles.mdx` states recurrence "was 12.9% at 12 months" (recurrence data were available for 147 patients, 19 events).
