reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:15:Numbers that appear on other WARWIKI pages and are not in the abstract, so they are NOT in the file: 423 patients with baseline data, 260 with 3-year renal data, 124 deaths, 39 without 3-year data, diversion-related reintervention 22% (T-pouch) versus 13% (Studer) with p<0.01, 44 cm detubularized reservoirs, Leadbetter/Bricker anastomoses, the list of reintervention causes (afferent-limb stenosis, stones, ureteral and urethral strictures), and the arm-specific UTI and late-complication figures. Also not captured: the follow-up of the 3-year endpoint's survivors, Clavien grades, operative details, eGFR denominators and CIs. Once the PDF is supplied, replace the three harm notes with n/N values and add the 423/260 denominators and the intervention incidence.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:17:## Disagreements and flags
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:18:- Pages (not edited) that use numbers I could not confirm from the abstract (all attributed to Skinner 2015): `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04c-urinary-diversion/t-pouch-modification.mdx` (423/260; 22% vs 13%, p<0.01; 44 cm reservoirs; Leadbetter/Bricker), `modified-studer-pouch.mdx` (423, 260, 124 deaths, 39 without data), `camey-ii-neobladder.mdx`, `double-t-pouch.mdx` (423/260; three-year cumulative incidence of secondary surgery), `bowel-segments.mdx` (237 vs 247 matches the abstract).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:19:- Confirmed from the abstract: 484 randomized (237 T-pouch, 247 Studer), Feb 2002 to Nov 2009, eGFR -6.6 vs -6.4 mL/min/1.73 m2, p=0.35, multivariable p=0.63, "mean eGFR change" wording (the abstract says "decreased by", not "mean"). Pages that call the change the "mean eGFR decline" are consistent with the direction.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:21:- Pages and the old Journal Club record call the pouches "Studer-type refluxing" and the trial "settled the reflux debate"; the abstract's conclusion is narrower (T-pouch did not prevent a moderate eGFR reduction at 3 years). Old record: "484" and "-6.4 vs -6.6" match; "added complexity" and "more secondary surgical procedures" are supported only as "increased diversion-related secondary surgery". The old `design: RCT` is correct; it omitted that the trial was single-center and unmasked.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:22:- Registry versus report: ClinicalTrials.gov lists 529 enrolled (actual) and a primary outcome covering renal function, upper-tract anatomy and need for medical or surgical intervention measured 3 years after the last patient enrolled; the report's primary endpoint is eGFR change from baseline to 3 years among 484 randomized. Not stated on the page.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/usc-star/notes.md:23:- Pagination: PubMed gives pp 433-439 (used, matches the site pages); Crossref gives 433-440. Ahmadi authors: Crossref/publisher lists Simma-Chiang as third author; PubMed lists six authors without her; the publisher list is used.

