docs/04-surgical-techniques/04g-prolapse-repair/posterior-enterocele/posterior-colporrhaphy.mdx:122:| In a randomized trial of 60 sexually active women without bothersome baseline dyspareunia undergoing posterior colporrhaphy (30 per arm), daily vaginal dilator use from postoperative weeks 4–8 did not significantly reduce de novo dyspareunia versus no dilator use (9.5% vs 19.2% at 3 months; 12.5% vs 3.8% at 6 months; neither difference significant), nor did it change PGI-I or PISQ-12 scores. The trial was underpowered (13% loss to follow-up) and does not test dilators for established dyspareunia or stenosis | <sup>[[27]](#ref27)</sup> |
