docs/03-clinical-conditions/03c-pelvic-support/pelvic-organ-prolapse.mdx:322:In the CARE trial, 12 of 313 stress-continent women leaked on urodynamics before sacrocolpopexy without prolapse reduction. With reduction at 300 mL, detection varied by method, from 6% with a pessary to 30% with a speculum. Women who leaked with reduction more often reported stress incontinence 3 months after surgery, both without a Burch colposuspension (58% vs 38%, p = 0.04) and with one (32% vs 21%, p = 0.19).<sup>[[39]](#ref39)</sup>
