docs/04-surgical-techniques/04g-prolapse-repair/posterior-enterocele/vaginal-mccall-culdoplasty.mdx:51:| **Modified McCall with extended dissection** (Ettore 2024) | USLs dissected to the ischial spines and shortened; at that level, 0 PDS sutures transfix each USL medial to lateral (the authors’ stated precaution against ureteral injury). The Douglas pouch is closed high, and suspension sutures attach to the vaginal apex and duplicated anterior and posterior fasciae.<sup>[[6]](#ref6)</sup> | In a prospective observational comparison, mean vaginal length 8.3 vs 6.4 cm at 12 months; any-compartment stage II or greater recurrence was 2/79 (2.5%) vs 5/75 (6.7%) among patients with complete 12-month follow-up (85 modified vs 86 traditional initially enrolled; the comparison group was an earlier cohort), described by the authors as a tendency toward lower recurrence<sup>[[6]](#ref6)</sup> |
