docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/liu-classification-hoodoplasty.mdx:113:The Xia and Liu classifications address different zones. In Xia’s Type 3 four-step group, junction hematomas occurred on 2/80 treated sides (2.5%) and required surgical evacuation.<sup>[[9]](#ref9)</sup> Liu subtypes the central zone (wide versus long). Xia subtypes the lateral-zone CLC and identifies the fused variant. In a nonrandomized historical comparison, later combined labial-and-hood four-step cases reported higher 3-month satisfaction than earlier labial wedge-only cases (33/36 versus 9/16 respondents); the comparison cannot isolate the effect of hood reduction.<sup>[[9]](#ref9)</sup>
