docs/04-surgical-techniques/04g-prolapse-repair/obliterative-pessary/colpocleisis-total.mdx:109:In a single-institution retrospective review of 210 Le Fort colpocleisis procedures, 161 women (77%) had a concurrent suburethral sling for overt or occult SUI; sling placement was associated with a 92.5% subjective stress-continent rate. Of the 56 patients presenting with voiding dysfunction, it resolved postoperatively in 91%, with de novo voiding dysfunction in 1.9% and sling revision in 0.6%. This is a single noncomparative cohort with median follow-up of 22 weeks.<sup>[[23]](#ref23)</sup>
