docs/04-surgical-techniques/04k-gender-affirming-surgery/genital-nullification-afab.mdx:45:**Nullification context.** Anterior vaginal wall flap preservation for urethral lengthening is not required (there is no phalloplasty or metoidioplasty target). Fulguration may be considered. In a retrospective single-institution comparison (Ho 2025; 70 patients, all with metoidioplasty), fulguration was associated with lower blood loss (88 vs 254 mL, p &lt; 0.01) and shorter operative time (183 vs 290 min, p &lt; 0.01) than epithelial excision in patients without hysterectomy.<sup>[[15]](#ref15)</sup> Vagino-cutaneous fistula rates were identical (10%), and vaginal remnant recurrence did not differ (5% vs 8%, p = 0.67).<sup>[[15]](#ref15)</sup> The Hougen 2020 technique paper describes the transperineal approach to sharp excision.<sup>[[16]](#ref16)</sup>
