docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/penuma.mdx:8:The **Penuma®** is an FDA-cleared subcutaneous silicone penile implant used for cosmetic augmentation; FDA has also cleared the distinct Augmenta penile implant for cosmetic correction of soft-tissue deformities.<sup>[[16]](#ref16)[[17]](#ref17)</sup> It received FDA 510(k) clearance as a Class II medical device<sup>[[23]](#ref23)</sup> and is a medical-grade soft-silicone crescent-shaped sleeve placed in the subcutaneous space around the penile shaft to increase girth and flaccid length. Published series report a 56.7% increase in midshaft circumference (single-surgeon series) and a 52% increase in flaccid length (single-center series).<sup>[[1]](#ref1)[[2]](#ref2)[[3]](#ref3)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/penuma.mdx:23:- **Material.** Medical-grade silicone elastomer with embedded polyester mesh in the FDA-cleared device; this solid implant is distinct from injected liquid silicone.<sup>[[16]](#ref16)</sup> The SMSNA strongly recommends against permanent penile fillers, including liquid silicone.<sup>[[16]](#ref16)[[6]](#ref6)</sup>
