docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/cryolipolysis.mdx:51:**Off-label suprapubic application.** The suprapubic / mons-pubis region is not specifically FDA-cleared for cryolipolysis. Azab reported suprapubic cryolipolysis but did not identify an applicator or cooling setting in the abstract; Mineroff's PubMed search found no additional clinical suprapubic study.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)[[13]](#ref13)</sup> Suprapubic treatment is outside CoolSculpting Elite's listed indications, and its manual prohibits placement on genitalia or inguinal creases.<sup>[[33]](#ref33)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/cryolipolysis.mdx:258:Cryolipolysis is an FDA-cleared noninvasive technology for localized fat reduction. Across non-suprapubic treatment sites, the Ingargiola review reported average reductions of 10.3–25.5% in ultrasound-measured fat-layer thickness and 14.67–28.5% in caliper-measured skinfold thickness. Pooled satisfaction was 80.4% among 479 participants in the Ravindran review; in Tan’s abdomen/flank study, 95/106 evaluable participants (89.6%) were satisfied or very satisfied 12 weeks after final treatment. Reported adverse events were mostly minor and self-limiting.<sup>[[3]](#ref3)[[14]](#ref14)[[15]](#ref15)</sup> Paradoxical adipose hyperplasia (PAH) is the main rare complication. Nikolis reported PAH incidence of 0.05–0.39% per treatment cycle, Cox reported 0.67% at one center among patients, and Mah pooled patient-level incidence at 0.22% (low-certainty evidence); the four Cox cases were treated surgically.<sup>[[27]](#ref27)[[25]](#ref25)[[32]](#ref32)</sup> Sex-based risk differences were not statistically significant in the pooled analysis.<sup>[[25]](#ref25)[[27]](#ref27)[[32]](#ref32)</sup> Patients are counseled about PAH before treatment.
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/cryolipolysis.mdx:260:For suprapubic fat reduction and apparent penile-length augmentation, cryolipolysis is a minimally studied noninvasive alternative to liposuction. In Azab 2021 (n = 46, single-arm), measurements made before sessions 1 and 3 differed by 0.99 cm in suprapubic skinfold thickness and 0.78 cm in apparent stretched penile length (both p &lt; 0.001); the abstract does not report a post-third-session measurement.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)</sup> The suprapubic area is not specifically FDA-cleared for cryolipolysis.<sup>[[13]](#ref13)</sup> Azab used three suprapubic sessions; the number needed for an individual patient and the relative effect versus surgery remain unknown.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)[[13]](#ref13)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04d-upper-tract-reconstruction/minimally-invasive/endoureterotomy.mdx:197:Endoureterotomy offers shorter operative time, less blood loss, faster recovery, and outpatient feasibility. Its cost is durability. Ou et al. found overall success of 51.6% for endourologic treatment compared with 95.7% for surgical reconstruction in benign ureteral strictures, in a retrospective, predominantly stone-related cohort.<sup>[[10]](#ref10)</sup> Zi et al. similarly found that balloon dilation could approximate reconstructive approaches early but lost ground at 12 and 24 months.<sup>[[31]](#ref31)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04d-upper-tract-reconstruction/pyelovesicostomy.mdx:108:| Pelvic kidney — open<sup>[[2]](#ref2)</sup> | 2 | 2/2 with sterile urine and stable renal function | Not reported in abstract | Residual dilatation persisted in one patient |
docs/05-special-populations/05a-trauma-emergencies/bladder-trauma.mdx:78:- Confirm healing with repeat cystography before catheter removal; EAU plans the first cystogram approximately 10 days after injury and gives a weak recommendation for conservative management of uncomplicated blunt extraperitoneal injury<sup>[[6]](#ref6)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/female-cosmetic.mdx:12:> **Society positions and evidence-quality caveat.** The ACOG 2020 Committee Opinion states that procedures to alter sexual appearance or function, other than those done for clinical indications, are not medically indicated, pose substantial risk, and have not had their safety and effectiveness established. The FIGO 2025 Statement holds that it is ethically inappropriate for obstetrician-gynecologists to recommend, perform or refer patients for cosmetic genital procedures in women without structural or functional abnormalities.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)[[4]](#ref4)</sup> The FDA 2018 safety communication warned against energy-based devices for "vaginal rejuvenation" and cosmetic indications; no such device is FDA-cleared for these uses.<sup>[[2]](#ref2)</sup> Assess psychological concerns during consultation; assess for **body dysmorphic disorder (BDD)** when indicated, and refer patients with suspected psychological concerns for mental-health evaluation before considering surgery.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/female-cosmetic.mdx:33:| **BDD screening** | Assess for BDD when indicated; refer patients with suspected psychological concerns for mental-health evaluation before considering surgery.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)</sup> BDDQ-AS was validated for screening in aesthetic rhinoplasty, not specifically female genital surgery; BDD-YBOCS assesses severity of current BDD.<sup>[[24]](#ref24)[[25]](#ref25)</sup> BDD affects about 2.5% of US adults.<sup>[[3]](#ref3)</sup> A systematic review estimated higher prevalence in general cosmetic-surgery settings than in community adults; this estimate is not specific to female genital surgery.<sup>[[26]](#ref26)</sup> |
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/female-cosmetic.mdx:75:Energy-based devices (fractional CO₂, Er:YAG, RF ± PEMF) are not FDA-cleared for cosmetic vaginal "rejuvenation" or for GSM (FDA 2018 Safety Communication).<sup>[[2]](#ref2)</sup> In the double-blind, sham-controlled Li 2021 *JAMA* RCT (85 postmenopausal women), fractional CO₂ laser did not significantly improve vaginal symptoms at 12 months.<sup>[[17]](#ref17)</sup> Uncontrolled series report benefit, and the discrepancy may reflect a placebo effect. A systematic review of vaginal-laxity treatments found improved sexual function in observational studies but not in randomized trials.<sup>[[11]](#ref11)</sup> FIGO 2025 states that research data are insufficient to support the safety and effectiveness of laser devices for GSM or cosmetic purposes.<sup>[[4]](#ref4)</sup> ESSM 2020 likewise found that the clinical effect of laser devices on vaginal symptoms was not clearly established.<sup>[[30]](#ref30)</sup> For GSM, the 2025 AUA/SUFU/AUGS guideline recommends counseling that evidence does not support CO₂ laser, Er:YAG laser, or radiofrequency for dryness, discomfort or irritation, dysuria, dyspareunia, quality of life, bothersome symptoms, or treatment satisfaction <Rec>(Moderate Recommendation; Grade C)</Rec>.<sup>[[29]](#ref29)</sup> It permits consideration of CO₂ laser for dryness, discomfort or irritation, dysuria, or dyspareunia in patients who are not candidates for, or prefer alternatives to, FDA-approved treatments, with shared decision-making and disclosure that use outside clinical trials is experimental <Rec>(Expert Opinion)</Rec>.<sup>[[29]](#ref29)</sup> A 2020 single-institution model used a $2,733 patient price for three CO₂ sessions; confirm current local pricing and payer coverage for counseling.<sup>[[40]](#ref40)</sup> For full cross-indication evidence (GSM / SUI / lichen sclerosus / vaginal laxity / breast-cancer survivors) see the canonical [Vaginal Laser Therapy](/docs/surgical-techniques/04f-incontinence-procedures/procedures/vaginal-laser-therapy) page.
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04l-cosmetic-genital-surgery/female-cosmetic.mdx:139:| [Vaginal Laser Therapy (Fractional CO₂ / Er:YAG / RF)](/docs/surgical-techniques/04f-incontinence-procedures/procedures/vaginal-laser-therapy) | Energy-Based Devices | GSM and "vaginal rejuvenation" uses are not FDA-cleared<sup>[[2]](#ref2)</sup>; a sham-controlled fractional CO₂ trial in postmenopausal women found no significant vaginal-symptom improvement at 12 months<sup>[[17]](#ref17)</sup> |
