docs/01-foundations/pharmacology/dermatologic-topical-urethral/platelet-rich-plasma.mdx:28:**Regulatory status.** In the United States, FDA-cleared platelet and plasma separators in the bone-graft-handling category prepare PRP for mixing with autograft or allograft bone.<sup>[[51]](#ref51)</sup> That device clearance does not establish an indication for injection into the bladder, urethra, corpora or genital skin.<sup>[[37]](#ref37)[[51]](#ref51)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04c-urinary-diversion/le-bag.mdx:74:Ileocolonic reservoirs can produce hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis. In the Kolettis cohort, median bicarbonate decreased from 28 to 24 mmol/L, with a reported association between pouch length and the biochemical change (r = 0.58). Persistent biochemical acidosis requires assessment even in the absence of symptoms; treatment depends on its severity, renal function and clinical context. See [Urinary Acidifiers & Alkalinizers](/docs/foundations/pharmacology/urinary-diversion-specific/urinary-acidifiers).<sup>[[4]](#ref4)</sup>
docs/04-surgical-techniques/04d-upper-tract-reconstruction/interposition-graft/bmg-onlay-ureter.mdx:182:**June 27, 2026 cohort.** Puri et al. retrospectively reviewed 40 patients at five centers; 95% met an endpoint combining improved imaging and no additional intervention at median 12.2 months, with 22.5% experiencing a 30-day complication. Inclusion required postoperative imaging. Selection bias, shorter follow-up and a different success definition prevent direct comparison with the 2025 cohort or ileal ureter. This adds support for selected onlay reconstruction without establishing lifelong patency.<sup>[[27]](#ref27)</sup>
