73 ### The PErFecTED technique
74 
75 **PErFecTED** (Proximal Embolization First, Then Embolize Distal) is a two-step approach described by Carnevale in 2014 to increase prostatic ischemia:<sup>[[11]](#ref11)</sup>
76 
77 1. **Step 1 (Proximal):** advance the microcatheter past collateral branches and position it within the prostatic artery before its branching; embolize slowly to near stasis. Selective embolization of the urethral group (which supplies the periurethral adenoma) precedes the capsular group after advancing into intraprostatic branches in Step 2.<sup>[[11]](#ref11)</sup>
78 2. **Step 2 (Distal).** At near stasis, inject contrast to check for newly apparent collateral shunts before advancing the microcatheter into intraprostatic branches. Slowly deliver additional embolic material to achieve distal stasis, avoiding reflux and injection through a wedged catheter. Retract to the arterial origin for the final control angiogram.<sup>[[11]](#ref11)</sup>
79 
80 The authors, in a technical report without a comparison group, described infarcts in all patients after adding the second step and lower recurrence than with earlier methods.<sup>[[11]](#ref11)</sup>
81 
82 ### Emerging adjuncts
83 
84 - **NBCA glue.** Loffroy 2026 (retrospective, n = 186): IPSS 20.1 to 10 at 12 mo; volume 118 to 81 mL; no major complications; IIEF-5 unchanged.<sup>[[13]](#ref13)</sup>
85 - **EVOH (Onyx-type).** Guerra 2026 (retrospective, n = 73): 88% clinical success at 3 mo; clinical success in all 57 patients with a high PEPS and none of 5 with a low PEPS.<sup>[[14]](#ref14)</sup>
86 - **"Coil-out".** Adjunctive coil occlusion of the prostatic artery after particle embolization to prevent recanalization has been described.<sup>[[5]](#ref5)</sup>
87 
88 The AUA 2026 guideline notes limited prospective evidence for liquid embolics.<sup>[[22]](#ref22)</sup>
