44 Laser-tissue interaction is temperature-dependent. Above 60°C, protein denatures and tissue coagulates, producing delayed tissue sloughing and prolonged postoperative dysuria; near the boiling point of water, about 100°C, tissue vaporizes, which is the goal of prostate ablative surgery because tissue is removed from the field immediately; above 150°C, tissue chars (carbonization).<sup>[[31]](#ref31)</sup>
