27-Discussion The consensus group recommends defining surgical success as anatomical closure of the fistula without residual
28-urinary incontinence, as closure alone is insufficient. Women with residual urinary incontinence should not be classified as
29:cured and require further diagnostic and therapeutic intervention. A postoperative dye test at catheter removal is advised
30-as an objective measure of surgical success. The group also underscores the importance of basic urodynamic evaluation to
31-assess residual incontinence following fistula closure. A diagnosis of “incurable” fistula should only be considered after
