reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:31:- `docs/01-foundations/tools/biomaterials/biological-grafts/porcine-sis.mdx` line 87: "PROSPECT randomized program (1,348 women followed to 6 years)". The 6-year report retained 65% of the 1,348 randomized women (IUJ 2023, Results, Participants and treatment); the next sentence of that page already says "about 65% response", so only the parenthetical is loose.
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:32:- `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04g-prolapse-repair/mesh-complications.mdx` line 73: "4.8% de novo severe (1/21 at 24 months); 13.0% severe overall (3/23 assessed at 24 months; PROSPECT mesh kits)". The percentages match the BJOG 2021 abstract; the denominators 1/21 and 3/23 could not be checked because the BJOG tables were not in the text available (arithmetic is consistent: 1/21 = 4.8%, 3/23 = 13.0%).
reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/prospect/notes.md:33:- `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04g-prolapse-repair/mesh-graft-augmented-repairs.mdx` line 53: "prolapse symptom scores ... were similar across randomized comparisons" at six years. True at 6 years (mesh trial mean difference 0.85, 95% CI -0.05 to 1.75; Table 1), but the 4-year mesh-trial POP-SS was higher after mesh (mean difference 1.01, 95% CI 0.20 to 1.83; P=0.015; below the 2-point threshold). The page does not mention 4 years, so no conflict unless the 4-year result is added.
