reports/2026-10-18/clinical-evidence/work/rosetta/notes.md:24:- `docs/04-surgical-techniques/04f-incontinence-procedures/procedures/sacral-neuromodulation.mdx:174` says, “the six-month difference is not a durable superiority claim.” The two-year analysis included **initial responders**, with outcome data for **260/298**, repeat injections and reprogramming; it did not retest the six-month primary comparison in the full randomized population. Source: Amundsen 2018, Methods and Results, clinical-responder population and Figure 2. A narrower statement is that no between-group episode difference was detected across 24 months among initial responders.
