docs/04-surgical-techniques/04f-incontinence-procedures/procedures/artificial-urinary-sphincter.mdx:149:The prospective, single-arm AUSCO trial implanted 115 men at 17 sites. At 12 months, 91/97 evaluable participants (94%) achieved ≥50% pad-weight reduction, while 61/101 (60%) reported zero pad use. Seventeen of 115 participants (15%) had a serious adverse event, including 10 (8.7%) with a serious device-related event; nine (7.8%) underwent revision, with none attributed to device infection. The Results report three wound infections, all resolving without erosion or explantation. Follow-up was one year after activation.<sup>[[12]](#ref12)</sup>
